# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-4 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-4 throughout: B4 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after B4's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# FX: the fix arm of the audits-off hang, c2-packed-tp4-speed-fix (gate only): c2-packed-tp4-speed (verify audits OFF, tail caps ON) plus
# the capture plug (QWEN_FAST_CAPTURE_PLUG=1, QWEN_FAST_CAPTURE_PLUG_ENGINES=1), the stall watch (QWEN_FAST_STALL_DEADLINE_S=120) and the
# collective handle guard in fail mode (QWEN_FAST_CCL_HANDLE_GUARD=1). The graph census is off. The hypothesis is allocation aliasing:
# a buffer allocated after a capture lands in a hole the capture freed, and a later replay overwrites it. The plug runs the packed
# captures inside a zone, plugs every hole they free with inert tensors, and keeps later allocations below it.
# The test list is T2's: v166's SS list in its order (concurrent4 then concurrent4_steady is the v164 sequence), then concurrent4_solo
# and replay_concurrent4 (the platform replay's request shape), then the two coding-text concurrency tests.
# READ the log: (1) no hang: every test returns, no stall line, no replay-deadline exit, the container alive at the end, every
# concurrent4 and concurrent4_steady user at 800 tokens, every replay_concurrent4 user at 300. (2) the plug lines: '[PINDIAG] capture
# plug packed' open, sealed and released once at attach, then one open and one sealed per engine build, and the monitor lines with
# free_mb never under the floor; no 'capture plug' error and no out-of-memory. (3) every content and reasoning hash equals B4's for the
# same test (the audits and the plug never change tokens): the fixed arm is token-identical to the audited arm. (4) report the round
# time SEPARATELY from the audits' 31 ms: live-4 packed verify median against c2-packed-tp4-speed's (the plug adds no device work to a
# round) and concurrent4 per-user mean against B4's. (5) the handle guard: no 'unfenced same-handle collective' line.
# Accepting the fix needs five consecutive passes of this job on this image, each after its own reset (see ORDER.txt). If a run stalls,
# the log holds '[STALL]' lines, every thread's stack and the triage tools' output before the process was ended: keep them.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min per run. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-4
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-fix
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
